@startuml
title Product Fulfillment and Activation Sequence Diagram

participant "TMFC002 Product Order\nCapture &\nValidation" as OrderCapture
participant "TMFC003 Product Order\nDelivery Orchestration &\nManagement" as OrderOrch
participant "TMFC005 Product Inventory" as ProductInventory
participant "TMFC001 Product Catalog\nManagement" as ProductCatalog
participant "Event Mgt" as EventMgt
participant "TMFC009 Service Qualification\nManagement" as ServiceQualification
participant "TMFC006 Service Catalog\nManagement" as ServiceCatalog
participant "TMFC008 Service Inventory" as ServiceInventory
participant "TMFC007 Service Order\nManagement" as ServiceOrder
participant "TMFC011 Resource Order\nManagement" as ResourceOrder
participant "TMFC010 Resource Catalog\nManagement" as ResourceCatalog
participant "TMFC012 Resource Inventory\nManagement" as ResourceInventory
participant "Resource Qualification" as ResourceQualification

note over OrderCapture, OrderOrch
  Continuing from the pre-order sequence diagram, the user has already placed the order, and CRM has already submitted the order together with the user-related information.
end note

== Step After Check Service Or Resource ==

note over OrderCapture
  Step 1: Customer Order Received
  Customer Order Processing Started
end note
OrderCapture -> OrderCapture : 1 Decompose Customer Order

loop for each productOrderItem
OrderCapture -> ProductCatalog : 2 TMF 620 Product Catalog Management\nGET /productSpecification
ProductCatalog --> OrderCapture : 3 TMF 620 200 productSpecification details
OrderCapture -> OrderCapture : 4 Validate Product Order
end

OrderCapture -> OrderCapture : 5 Update Product Order Statue
OrderCapture -> OrderOrch : 6 TMF622 ProductOrdering\nPOST /productOrder
OrderOrch -> OrderOrch : 7 start execution of productOrderItems
OrderOrch -> OrderOrch : 8 update productOrderItems\n(state="inProgress")
OrderOrch -> ProductInventory : 9 TMF637 Product Inventory Management\nPATCH /product\n(product-specification-level order items\nstate="Pending Active")
ProductInventory -> ProductInventory : 10 Process Product status

alt Can the product be reused?
ProductInventory --> OrderOrch : 11 Product is ready
OrderOrch --> OrderOrch : 12 Proceed to the product activation phase
OrderOrch -> OrderOrch : 13 Unpack the ProductOrder and prepare to proceed to the product activation phase. For details, refer to the next product activation
end

OrderOrch -> ProductCatalog : 14 TMF620 Product Catalog Management\nGET /productSpecification
ProductCatalog --> OrderOrch : 15 TMF620 200 productSpecification details, CFSSpecification,\nresourceSpecification, translationRules

== Service Level ==

OrderOrch -> ServiceOrder : 16 TMF641 Service Ordering\nPOST /serviceOrder
note over ServiceOrder : Service Orchestration Center receives the Service Order
ServiceOrder -> ServiceOrder : 17 validate Service order\n(state="acknowledged")
ServiceOrder --> OrderOrch : 18 TMF641 201 serviceOrder (state="acknowledged")
note over ServiceOrder : Service Orchestration Center starts parsing the CFS/RFS and their Specs
ServiceOrder -> ServiceOrder : 19 start execution of Service Order
ServiceOrder -> ServiceOrder : 20 update ServiceOrderItems(state="inProgress")
note over ServiceOrder : Service Orchestration Center starts analyzing the CFS content to identify all CFSs and RFSs.
ServiceOrder -> ServiceCatalog : 21 TMF633 Service Catalog Management\nGET /serviceSpecification
ServiceCatalog --> ServiceOrder : 22 TMF633 200 ServiceSpecification and ResourceSpecification
ServiceOrder -> ServiceOrder : 23 Organize all ServiceSpecifications and ResourceSpecifications

loop for each ServiceSpecification
ServiceOrder -> ServiceQualification : 24 TMF645 Service Qualification\nPOST /queryServiceQualification
ServiceQualification --> ServiceOrder : 25 TMF645 201 queryServiceQualification
ServiceOrder -> ServiceInventory : 26 TMF638 Service Inventory Management\nPOST /service (state="reserved")
ServiceInventory --> ServiceOrder : 27 TMF638 201 Service
end

note over ServiceOrder
  Service Orchestration Center parses all CFSs/RFSs to identify all Services.
  TMF633 has already been used above to identify all required ResourceSpecifications.
end note
ServiceOrder -> ServiceOrder : 28 Clarify which Services are ready
ServiceOrder -> ServiceOrder : 29 Clarify which Services depend on Resource Provision

== Resource Level ==

note over ServiceOrder : At the Service Level, identify the required Resources and place them into the Resource Order.
ServiceOrder -> ResourceOrder : 30 TMF652 Resource Order Management**\nPOST POST /resourceOrder
ResourceOrder -> ResourceOrder : 31 validate Resource order\n(state="acknowledged")
ResourceOrder --> ServiceOrder : 32 TMF652 201 resourceOrder (state="acknowledged")
ResourceOrder -> ResourceOrder : 33 start execution of Resource Order
ResourceOrder -> ResourceOrder : 34 update ResourceOrderItems(state="inProgress")
note over ResourceOrder : Start looking up the ResourceSpecifications and the corresponding Resources that need to be ready.
ResourceOrder -> ResourceCatalog : 35 TMF634 Resource Catalog Management\nGET /resourceCatalog
ResourceCatalog --> ResourceOrder : 36 TMF634 200 Resource Specification

loop for each ResourceSpecification
ResourceOrder -> ResourceQualification : 37 TMF761 Resource Qualification\nPOST /queryResourceQualification
ResourceQualification --> ResourceOrder : 38 TMF761 201 queryResourceQualification
end

ResourceOrder -> ResourceInventory : 39 TMF639 Resource Inventory Management\nPOST /resource (administrativeState="locked")
ResourceInventory --> ResourceOrder : 40 TMF639 201 Resource Inventory
ResourceOrder -> ResourceOrder : 41 All required Resources are ready
ResourceOrder -> ResourceOrder : 42 update ResourceOrderItems(state="completed")

ResourceOrder -> EventMgt : 43 TMF688 Event Management\nPOST event ResourceOrder\n(state="completed")
EventMgt -> ServiceOrder : 44 TMF688 Event Management\nPOST listener/resourceOrderStateChange\n(state="completed")
ServiceOrder -> ServiceOrder : 45 update ServiceOrderItems(state="completed")
ServiceOrder -> EventMgt : 46 TMF688 Event Management\nPOST event ServiceOrder\n(state="completed")
EventMgt -> OrderOrch : 47 TMF688 Event Management\nPOST listener/serviceOrderStateChange\n(state="completed")
OrderOrch -> OrderCapture : 48 Notify the user that the product is ready, and ask if they would like to activate it

note over OrderCapture
  1. 'completed' is passed back to the order because there is a risk of order cancellation; only after the product order is confirmed will it become 'active'.
  2. 'active' is equivalent to our archiving process.
end note

note over OrderCapture : After receiving the user's approval:
OrderCapture -> OrderOrch : 49 TMF622 Product Order Management\nPATCH /productOrder/{id}?fields=state (state="active")
OrderOrch -> OrderOrch : 50 update ProductOrderItems(state="active")
OrderOrch -> ServiceOrder : 51 TMF641 Service Order Management\nPATCH /serviceOrder/{id}?fields=state (state="active")
ServiceOrder -> ServiceOrder : 52 update ServiceOrderItems(state="active")
ServiceOrder -> ResourceOrder : 53 TMF652 Resource Order Management\nPOST POST /resourceOrder
ResourceOrder -> ResourceOrder : 54 update ResourceOrderItems(state="active")

loop Active Resource
ResourceOrder -> ResourceInventory : 55 TMF639 Resource Inventory Management\nPATCH /resource (administrativeState="active")
ResourceInventory -> ResourceInventory : 56 update Resource
ResourceInventory --> ResourceOrder : 57 TMF639 201 Resource Inventory
end

ResourceOrder --> ServiceOrder : 58 TMF652 201 resourceOrder (state="active")

loop Active Service
ServiceOrder -> ServiceInventory : 59 TMF638 Service Inventory Management\nPATCH /service (state="active")
ServiceInventory -> ServiceInventory : 60 update Service
ServiceInventory --> ServiceOrder : 61 TMF638 201 Service Inventory
end

ServiceOrder --> OrderOrch : 62 TMF641 201 Service Order

loop Active Product
OrderOrch -> ProductInventory : 63 TMF637 Product Inventory Management\nPATCH /product (state="active")
ProductInventory -> ProductInventory : 64 update Product
ProductInventory --> OrderOrch : 65 TMF637 201 Product Inventory
end

OrderOrch --> OrderCapture : 66 TMF622 201 Product Order
note over OrderCapture : 1. Notify the user that the product has been successfully activated and is now ready for use.
@enduml
